// Scope: idempotency lens — algebraic-law-derived; redundant ops collapse structurally.
// Anchor: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Idempotence
// Unifies: (per THESIS:188) idempotency + cancellation + redundancy = algebraic simplification. Three named runtime concerns are ONE mechanism. A worker hitting "I need cancellation" or "I need redundancy detection" extends THIS lens, not new lens/cancellation.dag or lens/redundancy.dag.
//
// Owns:
//   - lens read: Node -> Witness<IdempotencyClaim>
//   - composes with std/algebra.dag for law-derived simplification
//
// Consumes:
//   - std/node.dag, std/algebra.dag, std/witness.dag
//
// Status: scaffold — fill per TASKS.md T-13
// Brief: see BRIEF_TEMPLATE.md; this file's I/O contract is the immutable
